---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/sendlane-alternative';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'alternatives/sendlane-alternative');
const desc = description(site, 'alternatives/sendlane-alternative');

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does the acquisition mean Sendlane has shut down?",
    "answer": "The Privy acquisition announcement does not establish shutdown or an automatic transfer for every account. Obtain an account-specific continuity plan from the incumbent."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is a good reason to stay?",
    "answer": "A confirmed plan preserving account access, creative workflows, campaigns, support ownership and acceptable costs can avoid unnecessary rebuilding."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a replacement demonstration include?",
    "answer": "Use your real campaign brief and proposed capture, creative approval, reply escalation, purchase exit and queue cancellation fixtures. Compare the service workload as well as the software."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I copy the subscriber list and start sending?",
    "answer": "List import alone does not preserve permission, current withdrawals, journey state or old queued sends. Reconcile these and assign one production owner before activating the affected work."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/alternatives" class="link text-sm">← All alternatives</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Sendlane alternatives: decide around account, creative and service continuity</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl">Choose the scope of change from the work your team needs to preserve. Current supplier positioning checked November 25, 2026; account terms and acceptance results must come from your own review.</p>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>What the acquisition changes in this decision</h2>
      <p><a href="https://www.privy.com/sendlane-acquisition">Privy confirms its acquisition of Sendlane</a> and describes a combined direction spanning email, SMS and onsite marketing. That provides a positive reason to discuss continuity and consolidated services with the incumbent. It does not establish that every account, contract, sender number or automation transfers automatically. It also does not establish a shutdown. This guide proposes account and workflow acceptance work; it reports no performed migration test or merchant outcome.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Ask the incumbent for an account-specific continuity plan</h2>
      <p>Before rebuilding anything, request the current product destination, login and administrator model, billing entity, renewal terms, support route and named handover owner for your account. Ask what continues unchanged, what needs rebuilding and which dates are commitments rather than roadmap expectations. Retain a written inventory of existing automations, creatives, reports and integrations. A confirmed support and service plan can make staying the least disruptive choice; acquisition alone is neither a reason to leave nor evidence that all work has been done.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Compare staying, repairing and moving the service</h2>
      <p>Keep the account if the team can preserve campaigns, support coverage and economics. Repair a broken integration, stale offer or missing operator before replacing the whole platform. If the actual problem is creative capacity, compare a managed service arrangement and an agency handover against a software switch. Move sending only if capture and creative workflows can remain dependable. A full replacement should have an acceptance plan for acquisition, campaigns, automation and service responsibilities together.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Candidates should solve the documented gap</h2>
      <p><a href="https://www.omnisend.com/">Omnisend</a> presents ecommerce email, SMS, web push and automation; evaluate it when one team wants to coordinate those campaigns. <a href="https://postscript.io/">Postscript</a> presents SMS, email, onsite opt-in and a managed strategy service; evaluate the division of work when reply coverage or execution capacity is central. Ask each to demonstrate the actual campaign brief, revision process and support escalation. These are reasons to investigate, not proof of feature parity, a rank or guaranteed savings. There is no requirement to add a separate lifecycle supplier.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Account and access acceptance comes before production changes</h2>
      <p>Build a proposed role matrix for store owner, marketer, designer, agency and support operator. Verify who can approve content, change billing, export permission records, cancel sends and revoke old credentials. Record connected storefronts, API clients, webhooks, tracking domains, reply addresses and sender-number ownership. Obtain account-specific confirmation of any number transfer or service transition and its dependencies. Keep an export and an accountable contact for unresolved items; a new login alone does not prove old queued work or billing has stopped.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Hand over creative as usable campaigns</h2>
      <p>For a proposed seasonal product launch, retain source designs, approved copy, image rights, translations, mobile layouts, alt text and brand rules. Record offer terms, coupon expiry, inventory constraints and the approval history. Recreate links, tracking parameters and dynamic product blocks with controlled recipients before scheduling. Include an out-of-stock variant and a gift purchaser who should receive care instructions rather than a self-replenishment offer. Agree who supplies assets, requests revisions and signs off on the final email and SMS versions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Preserve acquisition and audience intent</h2>
      <p>Inventory checkout collection, forms, keywords, landing pages and any agency-managed placements. Capture each disclosure version, source, timestamp, destination list and promised frequency. Demonstrate how a repeat signup, changed email or reused phone is resolved without resetting an opt-out. Retain segment definitions for VIP access, prior purchasers, wholesale buyers and open support cases rather than exporting only current members. A service handover must identify who updates live forms and disclosures; leaving an old form connected can silently repopulate the wrong audience.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Service coverage needs a realistic exercise</h2>
      <p>Propose a subscriber replying to a campaign with a delivery problem, another asking for HELP and another opting out while a promotion is queued. Assign response ownership, escalation route, hours of coverage and a fallback if the agency or supplier is unavailable. Keep unresolved support tickets visible to campaign operators. Define which messages should pause for an open case and which operational notices still apply. Check local-time scheduling, unknown timezone handling and destination requirements with appropriate review before activating marketing; the exercise is not a legal assurance.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Move a campaign and a journey without duplicate sends</h2>
      <p>Choose a disabled welcome journey and a cart reminder as proposed fixtures. Record existing enrollment, scheduled messages, purchase exit rules, limits and cancellation IDs. Import history without enrolling everyone again. Replay the same checkout twice, then deliver a purchase or withdrawal after enrollment but before dispatch; expect deduplication and the appropriate cancellation. Pause old writers and reconcile their queues before enabling a new production owner. On failure, stop the affected sends, resolve both queues and restore the approved path without resending fulfilled offers. Automatic account transfer must never be assumed to do this work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Judge economics including the service handover</h2>
      <p>Get ordinary and peak-season quotes for equal audience sizes, destinations, SMS segments, MMS creative, emails, carrier and number fees, modules, overages and contract terms. Include creative revisions, managed services, reply staffing, migration labor and any overlap charge. A hypothetical $100 sale with $45 fixed goods cost and $10 other variable cost leaves $45; applying a $25 incentive leaves $20, not a universal loss. Thirty incremental orders at $20 yield $600 before a $450 campaign cost, leaving $150 before labor and fixed costs. Discounts do not make goods cheaper. Use a suitable holdout to estimate incrementality, and review refunds, full-price repeats and opt-outs by campaign rather than treating attributed revenue as profit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Make the handover decision explicit</h2>
      <p>Stay if the account plan, creative process and service coverage meet your needs. Replace only the failing scope when that preserves useful work. For a full move, require approved creatives, live capture ownership, permission reconciliation, current purchase checks, support coverage and verified queue control before release. Schedule with the people who can resolve failures present, and record rollback authority. The separate <a href="/alternatives/sequenzy-alternative">Sequenzy guide</a> focuses on product and Stripe event dependencies; those are not a substitute for this account and service acceptance record.</p>
    </div>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="FAQ: Sendlane alternatives" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
